---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://uncrashableholdings.com');
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', url: site.toString() }];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Uncrashable Holdings"
  description="Uncrashable doesn't mean nothing bad will happen. It means that when it does, what you built doesn't die in the wreck."
  crumbs={crumbs}
  isHome
>
  <div class="hero">
    <svg
      class="signal"
      width="320"
      height="96"
      viewBox="0 0 1000 300"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      role="img"
      aria-label="A steady line dips once, then rises above its baseline."
    >
      <line x1="80" y1="90" x2="80" y2="150" stroke="#3B3F6B" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="butt" />
      <line x1="80" y1="150" x2="240" y2="150" stroke="#3B3F6B" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="butt" />
      <path class="oxblood" d="M 240 150 L 280 190 L 320 150" stroke="#5C1A1B" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill="none" />
      <line x1="320" y1="150" x2="400" y2="150" stroke="#3B3F6B" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="butt" />
      <path class="gold" d="M 400 150 L 440 110 L 480 150" stroke="#C9A227" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill="none" />
      <line x1="480" y1="150" x2="830" y2="150" stroke="#3B3F6B" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="butt" />
    </svg>

    <h1>Uncrashable doesn't mean nothing bad will happen.</h1>

    <p>It means that when it does, and it will, what you built doesn't die in the wreck.</p>

    <p class="dim">Continuity matters more than appearance. What still works when life stops cooperating?</p>

    <div class="direct-answer">
      <p>
        Most planning asks how to optimize what already exists. Fewer ask what happens if the thing holding it all together disappears. That question has a name:
        <a href="/framework/invisible-fragility">Invisible Fragility</a>, the gap between looking stable and actually being able to withstand disruption.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Uncrashable Holdings built <a href="/framework/aoidr">AOIDR</a> to diagnose it, five pillars, one framework, examined at increasing depth through the
      <a href="/diagnostics">diagnostics</a> that follow.
    </p>

    <p>
      The framework applies differently depending on where you stand. <a href="/verticals">Explore how it applies</a> to your world.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-line">
      <p>
        Start with the <a href="/diagnostics/continuity-scan" class="action">Continuity Scan</a>. Five questions. No score. No diagnosis. Just the first honest look.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="about-line">
      <a href="/about">Read more about the practitioner behind this framework.</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: 2.5rem; }
  .signal { display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .signal path { stroke-dasharray: 400; stroke-dashoffset: 400; animation: draw 2.2s ease-out forwards; }
  .signal path.oxblood { animation-delay: 0.1s; }
  .signal path.gold { animation-delay: 0.9s; }
  @keyframes draw { to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .signal path { animation: none; stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  }
  .hero h1 { font-weight: 500; font-size: 2.1rem; max-width: 22ch; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .dim { color: var(--cream-dim); }
  .direct-answer { border-left: 2px solid var(--indigo-deep); padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0; }
  .direct-answer p { font-weight: 500; }
  .cta-line { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(122, 128, 196, 0.25); }
  .about-line { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .hero h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; } }
</style>
